REQUEST_VERSION 1.0.0

ID REQUEST-0011

STATUS PENDING

DATE 2026-07-25

WHO President Cley Duarte

SCOPE PACE

TITLE

Install/intake must be an intelligent, multi-source onboarding: quick code
review plus the questions it deems fit; greenfield context questions when
there is no code; document ingestion with confirm-what-was-deduced; and
optional connection to ClickUp or GitHub -- always confirming deductions
with the owner before anything becomes official.

RAW_TEXT

PACE must have an instruction, at install time, to do a quick review of the
code and ask the client whatever questions it deems appropriate. If the
code is new, have questions that give it context too. It should also be
able to receive documents to analyze and ask or confirm what it deduced, or
connect to ClickUp or GitHub to find out.

PROPOSED_SCOPE PACE

DESIGN_NOTE

Expands the guided Intake (pace init --guided) into a multi-source engine:
  (1) EXISTING CODE -- quick review, propose a first draft of mission /
      vision / roadmap.
  (2) GREENFIELD (no code) -- a context questionnaire so it still gets
      grounded.
  (3) DOCUMENTS the client provides -- analyze them and confirm what was
      deduced.
  (4) CONNECTORS -- optionally pull context from ClickUp (roadmap, tasks)
      and GitHub (repo, issues, history).
In every path the AI PROPOSES and the owner (ROOT_AUTHORITY) confirms
before it is written as official -- Governance rule 1.

PROMOTED_TO

(pending)

APPROVED_BY

(pending)

END
